# @kintsugi/store/git — commit-as-fold at git-projection altitude.
#
# THE TERMINAL TICK of the N-cascade. `mirror kintsugi --commit` IS
# `git commit` at git-projection altitude. Every settle folds over
# the verdict cache; every git commit IS a projection of the
# substrate's transformation state to git-projection altitude; every
# rebase walks `impacted_by` over the fold.
#
# Interpretation B canonical DOES apply (green-field species,
# narrative-above `---` seam, `in @...` clauses below).
#
# === The N-cascade positioning ===
#
# This species closes the N-cascade landed 2026-07-05 → 2026-07-07:
#
#   N1 (`2857fb1`) — `@epistemologic/property/verdict_is_content_addressed`
#                    declared verdict = f(spec_oid, target_oid,
#                    inputs_oid) as a total function of its three
#                    OID inputs. Memoization becomes valid by
#                    construction.
#   N2 (`0a72c42`) — `@mirror/store/action_cache` species declared
#                    `cache_read` / `cache_write` / `cache_exists`
#                    at the three-OID key surface. The REAPI
#                    ActionCache floor at substrate altitude. The
#                    fold SUBJECT of commit_as_fold.
#   N3 (`756f2f7`) — Rust wiring in `cmd_kintsugi_spec` at
#                    `bootstrap/src/lib.rs` — `cache_read` before
#                    cargo dispatch, `cache_write` after each fresh
#                    verdict. The action_cache goes live.
#   N4 (`6bf05cb`) — `impacted_by(oid) -> [oid]` reverse-closure at
#                    @mirror/store family-root. The REBASE WALK
#                    subject: given a touched OID, name every
#                    downstream OID whose cached verdict may be
#                    affected. Surgical invalidation.
#   N5 (this tick) — `commit_as_fold` at @kintsugi/store/git.
#                    Projects the whole cascade to git.
#
# **Business-observable outcome**: every `mirror kintsugi --commit`
# folds the verdict cache into a git commit. Every git rebase walks
# `impacted_by` over the fold to determine which cache entries
# invalidate. The substrate's persistence layer IS git via
# `@mirror/store/git`; the substrate's transformation layer IS the
# kintsugi fold via this species. Together: commit-as-fold = cli
# verb + species action pair.
#
# === Form/process partition (Recognition #55) ===
#
# `[[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]` (#55)
# names the substrate's top-level partition: @mirror declares the
# form (state, observation, structure); @kintsugi declares the
# process (transformation, mutation, dynamics). This species sits
# on the @kintsugi (process) side of the partition, sibling to
# `@mirror/store/git` (form / state-observation side).
#
# `commit_as_fold` IS the transformation — the fold operation that
# takes a batch of verdict-cache writes and settles them into one
# content-addressed commit. `@mirror/store/git.set_ref` IS the
# state mutation the transformation discharges to — the fold's
# result is a new commit OID that the sibling species' `set_ref`
# writes to `HEAD` (or the caller-supplied ref name).
#
# The partition is one symbol deep: the transformation lives here
# under @kintsugi; the state-mutation lives under @mirror. Neither
# contains the other. commit_as_fold reads the action_cache carrier
# (N2), consults impacted_by (N4) for rebase-walk semantics, and
# discharges the settled fold through @mirror/store/git.set_ref.
# Three species boundaries; one composition.
#
# === Recognition #43 grounding (mirror IS content-addressed build system) ===
#
# `[[architecture-mirror-as-content-addressed-build-system]]` (#43;
# LANDED at M6 TICK 1 `884f433`): mirror has every Bazel / Buck2 /
# Nix / Shake primitive declared at substrate altitude. The commit-
# as-fold primitive was declared at Bazel's REAPI floor as the
# ActionResult-batch-write discipline (the settlement of an action
# batch into one content-addressed artifact); mirror's altitude-4
# form of the same primitive lives HERE at @kintsugi/store/git.
#
# This closes the terminal Bazel-REAPI-floor-decomposition
# sub-prism: N2 landed the ActionCache read/write; N5 lands the
# batch settlement that folds N2's writes into a single content-
# addressed commit. Recognition #43's chain (#43 → N1 → N2 → N3 →
# N4 → N5) is now closed at the git-projection altitude.
#
# === Third witness: cli-verb-pair-specialises-species-action-pair ===
#
# Candidate recognition `cli-verb-pair-specialises-species-action-pair`:
#
#   Witness 1: `spawn/kintsugi` ⇔ `@song/movement.enter/close` (M2 TICK 2)
#   Witness 2: (waiting)
#   Witness 3 (THIS TICK): `mirror kintsugi --commit` ⇔
#                          `@kintsugi/store/git.commit_as_fold`
#
# The recognition is that each cli-verb PAIR (a verb + its modifier
# flag, e.g. `kintsugi --commit`) specialises a species-action PAIR
# (a species + its action, e.g. `@kintsugi/store/git.commit_as_fold`).
# The specialisation is bidirectional: the cli-verb pair addresses
# the species-action pair through the standard cli-to-substrate
# dispatch surface; the species-action pair discharges through the
# cli-verb pair's operational shape (arguments, environment, exit
# code). Landing this species PROMOTES the recognition from
# CANDIDATE to LANDED via this third witness.
#
# === Third witness: cross-species-discharge-is-first-class ===
#
# Candidate recognition `cross-species-discharge-is-first-class`:
#
#   Witness 1: N3 `cmd_kintsugi_spec` calling
#              `@mirror/store/action_cache` (`cmd_kintsugi_spec` at
#              bootstrap altitude discharging into store species).
#   Witness 2: N4 `impacted_by` → `action_cache` invalidation
#              composition (family-root reverse-closure discharging
#              into species-altitude cache surface).
#   Witness 3 (THIS TICK): `commit_as_fold` composes N2
#              `@mirror/store/action_cache` (fold subject) + N4
#              `impacted_by` at @mirror/store family-root (rebase
#              walk) + `@mirror/store/git.set_ref` (state discharge)
#              across THREE species boundaries in one action.
#
# The recognition is that cross-species discharge — an action in
# one species composing actions from multiple other species — is
# first-class at the substrate-decl surface where all agree on the
# canonical types (`oid`, `verdict`, `imperfect`, `crystal`).
# commit_as_fold names the composition IN BODY through the
# obligation block; the realisation layer discharges each cited
# action against its declared species. Landing this species
# PROMOTES the recognition from CANDIDATE to LANDED via this third
# witness.
#
# === The commit-as-fold semantics ===
#
# `commit_as_fold(commit_message, ref_name)` performs the terminal
# settlement of a kintsugi-loop batch:
#
#   1. FOLD over `@mirror/store/action_cache`'s pending verdict
#      writes since the previous fold. The fold is left-to-right
#      per REAPI's `ActionResult` sequence order; each write
#      contributes one entry to the batch's derived_predicates
#      delta.
#   2. Compute the batch's content-address via the six-op
#      `write(bytes)` at @mirror/store — this produces the new
#      commit OID.
#   3. Consult `@mirror/store.impacted_by(prev_head_oid)` to
#      determine the rebase-walk closure of downstream OIDs whose
#      cached verdicts may be affected by the fold. The result IS
#      the invalidation set the next kintsugi tick uses.
#   4. Discharge the state mutation via
#      `@mirror/store/git.set_ref(ref_name, new_commit_oid)` —
#      atomic pointer update on the git ref (typically `HEAD`).
#   5. Return an `imperfect` carrying the new commit oid on
#      success or opacity on any step's failure.
#
# The three-species composition — N2 action_cache (fold subject) +
# N4 impacted_by (rebase walk) + @mirror/store/git.set_ref (state
# discharge) — is first-class per the second candidate recognition
# above. commit_as_fold IS the substrate-decl'd bridge between
# transformation (kintsugi's fold) and state (git's ref).
#
# === Operational target: `mirror kintsugi --commit` ===
#
# Business context: after N3 landed, the pre-commit hook's kintsugi
# pass memoizes verdicts through the action_cache. But those
# writes accumulate at cache altitude; they need a batch settlement
# to be observable at git-projection altitude (i.e., seen by
# `git log`, propagated via `git push`, walked by `git rebase`).
#
# `mirror kintsugi --commit` is the cli verb pair that dispatches
# this species' `commit_as_fold` action. On invocation:
#
#   - Reads the accumulated action_cache writes since last fold.
#   - Folds them into a batch content-address.
#   - Consults impacted_by on the prior head OID for rebase-walk
#     closure.
#   - Writes the new commit OID via @mirror/store/git.set_ref.
#   - Emits the settled commit oid to the caller.
#
# The kintsugi loop's beat is now observable at git-projection
# altitude. `git log` walks the fold history; `git rebase` walks
# impacted_by over the fold; `git push` propagates the batch.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Bazel REAPI ActionResult-batch
#                          `github.com/bazelbuild/remote-apis` —
#                          the `Execute` RPC's batch-of-actions
#                          settlement pattern; folds a sequence of
#                          `Action` invocations into one
#                          `ActionResult`-batch cached under one
#                          content-address. commit_as_fold is the
#                          substrate-altitude form at the git
#                          projection.
#   Git commit-as-tree     git's own commit-object is a tree-fold:
#                          the commit-object OID is computed by
#                          hashing the tree OID + parent OID(s) +
#                          author + message. commit_as_fold is the
#                          substrate-altitude form of the same
#                          fold, projected to git via
#                          @mirror/store/git.set_ref.
#   Nix ca-derivations     Dolstra 2020-2023: the ca-derivation arc
#                          treats each derivation's output as a
#                          content-addressed fold of its inputs.
#                          The fold at derivation altitude
#                          parallels commit_as_fold at kintsugi
#                          altitude.
#   Left-fold (foldl)      Bird & Wadler (1988) `Introduction to
#                          Functional Programming` — the fold
#                          operator is the canonical batch-
#                          settlement primitive over a sequence of
#                          effects. commit_as_fold names the
#                          substrate's left-fold over verdict-cache
#                          writes.
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per [[feedback-substrate-pull]]: every carrier below rides a
# type the substrate already declared. Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]:
# every action parameter is a typed newtype (`oid` from @mirror/store,
# `ref_name` from @mirror/store/git, `imperfect` from @glass); no
# bare primitives escape. Per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]:
# the five-operation prism block IS the canonical declaration
# form. Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]: the
# commit-as-fold primitive rides the substrate's existing fold
# discipline (@mirror/store six-op + @mirror/store/git set_ref +
# @mirror/store/action_cache) without inventing new vocabulary.
#
# === Path-namespace property ===
#
# This file at `shards/kintsugi/store/git.mirror` declares
# `@kintsugi/store/git` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`. Depth-2 sub-prism
# under @kintsugi (family-root); sibling name-shape to
# `@mirror/store/git` under @mirror (the form-side partition).
#
# Spec context:
#              `docs/specs/mirror-store.md` (the family-root
#               surface @mirror/store declares; the six-op floor
#               commit_as_fold discharges to via @mirror/store/git);
#              `docs/specs/mosaic-store-cache-invariants.md` (Mara
#               2026-06-28; §9.2 forward-promises the commit-as-fold
