---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @kintsugi
in @mirror/store
in @mirror/store/git
in @mirror/store/action_cache

# === The @kintsugi/store/git sub-prism ===
#
# Per the form/process partition (#55): @kintsugi is process-side
# (transformation, mutation, dynamics); @mirror/store/git is form-
# side (state observation at git-wire altitude). This species
# inherits from @kintsugi at family-root altitude. Sibling name-
# shape to @mirror/store/git under @mirror.
#
# The five-operation gauge action at this species' altitude
# operates over `commit_fold` — the typed handle for one open
# batch-fold session bridging the action_cache to the git wire.
prism @kintsugi/store/git <= @kintsugi {
  focus commit_fold
  project commit_fold
  split commit_fold
  shift commit_fold
  settle commit_fold
}

# === The commit_fold handle ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming one open
# batch-fold session. Bridges the action_cache carrier (fold
# subject) to the git wire (state discharge). Realisation layer
# binds the underlying carrier.
#
# Construction: implicit via the family-root's `settle` at this
# altitude once a crystal head + git store are bound. Equality is
# realisation-instance identity, not content-identity.
type commit_fold = ref

# === commit_message — the batch settlement description ===
#
# The message string attached to the fold's resulting git commit.
# Lifted from the substrate scalar floor as a typed reference per
# the [[feedback-no-bare-types]] discipline; naming distinguishes
# commit-message strings from arbitrary strings at the type level.
type commit_message = ref(scalar/string)

# === commit_as_fold — THE TERMINAL N-CASCADE ACTION ===
#
# THE FOLD-AND-COMMIT SUBSTRATE PRIMITIVE. Given a batch settlement
# request (commit message + target ref name), perform the terminal
# settlement of the kintsugi-loop batch:
#
#   1. FOLD over @mirror/store/action_cache's pending verdict
#      writes since the previous fold. The fold IS a content-
#      address computation: writes → new derived_predicates oid.
#   2. Consult @mirror/store.impacted_by on the prior head OID to
#      determine the rebase-walk closure of downstream OIDs whose
#      cached verdicts may be affected. Names the invalidation set.
#   3. Discharge state mutation via
#      @mirror/store/git.set_ref(ref_name, new_commit_oid). Atomic
#      pointer update at the git wire altitude.
#
# The composition — N2 action_cache (fold subject) + N4
# impacted_by (rebase walk) + @mirror/store/git.set_ref (state
# discharge) — is first-class at the substrate-decl surface where
# all three species agree on `oid`. Cross-species discharge is
# first-class per the third-witness recognition promoted this tick.
#
# The wire's standard imperfect return per @glass's `imperfect(a,
# e, l)` floor:
#
#   success(commit_oid: oid) — FOLD SETTLED. The new commit oid
#                              is live at the target ref; git log
#                              observers see it.
#   partial(opacity_map)     — FOLD PARTIAL. Some writes settled
#                              but ref-update contended (rare;
#                              parallels @mirror/store.write
#                              semantics).
#   failure(reason)          — FOLD FAILED. Caller retries or
#                              bails; the action_cache carrier is
#                              unchanged (transactional invariant).
#
# The obligation block `{ \ }` discharges at the realisation
# boundary through the three cited actions.
commit_as_fold(msg: commit_message, ref: ref_name) -> imperfect { \ }

out @kintsugi/store/git
out commit_fold
out commit_message
out commit_as_fold
